@page "/config"

<PageTitle>Configuration | Blazorade Static Pages</PageTitle>
<StaticPage Title="@title">
    
    <h1>@title</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Apps using Blazorade Static Pages are configured at build time with a
        <code>blazorade.config.json</code> file in the application's project root.
    </p>

    <p>
        The file is placed alongside the consuming Blazor WebAssembly project file. Static Pages
        reads its own settings from the <code>staticPages</code> section; the runtime application
        does not load this file.
    </p>

    <h2>Example</h2>

    <pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>{
  "staticPages": {
    "siteUrl": "https://www.example.com"
  }
}</code></pre>

    <p>
        The <code>siteUrl</code> value is the public site origin used when generating canonical URLs
        and other metadata for discovered routes. For example, a component with the route
        <code>/products</code> produces the canonical URL
        <code>https://www.example.com/products</code>.
    </p>

    <p>
        The shared configuration file can contain sections for other Blazorade libraries as well.
        Each library reads only its own section, so settings remain isolated.
    </p>
</StaticPage>
